# Story 59: Web Search (40s)
# Hook: Ask the agent to search the web -- web_search hits the Brave Search API, no approval needed.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-059-web-search.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Ask the agent to search the web -- web_search hits the Brave Search API, no approval needed.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh. Make sure your Brave API key is set so web_search is enabled.

[00:08.0 --> 00:13.0]
Double-press Escape for prompt mode.

[00:13.0 --> 00:32.0]
Ask it to look something up. The web_search tool queries the Brave Search API and feeds the results back to the agent, which summarizes them right in the pane. It's read-only, so it runs without an approval prompt.

[00:32.0 --> 00:37.0]
Web search is off until you set brave_api_key in your config, or the RYSH_BRAVE_API_KEY environment variable -- then every pane can reach the web.

[00:37.0 --> 00:40.0]
The agent's reach extends past your machine -- straight to the web.

